new file mode 100644
index 00000000..07af88ef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/1230.change.md
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+`AttributeError`s that are raised by properties (or any other descriptors) of slotted classes with `functools.cached_property`s are not replaced by a generic "object has no attribute" error anymore.
+
+To achieve that, slotted cached properties are now implemented as descriptors that fill their slot, instead of a class-wide `__getattr__` that would be called for *every* failing attribute access.
